{0 workero}

Write Cloudflare Workers in OCaml. workero compiles your program to WebAssembly
with wasm_of_ocaml and provides OCaml interfaces to runtime APIs and Cloudflare
bindings.

Handlers run in direct style. Calls such as [Workero.fetch] wait for their
result while the runtime handles other requests.

{1 Get started}

- {{!page-getting_started}Getting started}: create a Worker, run it locally, and deploy it.
- {{!page-template}The project template}: files, build configuration, and example routes.

{1 Runtime APIs}

Use {{!page-runtime_apis}Runtime APIs} to register handlers, route HTTP
requests, return responses, stream data, open TCP connections, receive email,
and run background work.

{1 Bindings}

{{!page-bindings}Bindings} expose configuration and Cloudflare resources through
your handler's [env] argument. Use them for storage, Durable Objects, Queues,
other Workers, static assets, databases through Hyperdrive, AI, analytics, and
rate limiting. {{!page-entrypoints}Entrypoints} expose RPC methods that other
Workers call through a service binding, and {{!page-workflows}Workflows} run
durable multi-step programs.

